styles.engine:
Good fit for grayscale mask tinting. Team colour is confined to the cap, overalls, reservoir, roller sleeve and paint, and the sheet's pink and green palette swap shows the separation works. Runtime surface paint suits stamped splat, coat and drip textures into a per-surface mask. The drips that hang below the platform edge need their own decal layer rather than only top-face coverage. The look depends on shaders the concept fakes with SVG filters:
(1) a full-screen canvas grain plus luminance-derived impasto relief pass;
(2) a gloss or specular pass on the paint layer only, ideally a height or normal derived from the paint mask so new paint gets the wet sheen automatically;
(3) optionally a low-frequency edge-wobble displacement on the world layer.
All three are cheap fragment passes, but they are new renderer work in Labrador (a post-process chain and a paint-layer material) that the d3d11 path would need. Without them the result collapses to flat cartoon shapes.
